  <content class="appendix">
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Data Set A: Raindrop Positions on a 3-Inch String (n = 47)</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Data type: SIMULATED — these values were computer-generated for classroom use, not collected from real people or events.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><link url="https://openstax.org/r/stats-excel-data-set-a">Link to Excel Version of Data</link></para>
      <para id="para-00003">A 3-inch piece of string is taped to the ground before a rainstorm, with its left end marked 0 and its right end marked 3 (see the picture below). During a 1-minute storm, the position (in inches from the left end) of every raindrop that hit the string was recorded. Because any point on the string is equally likely to be hit, positions were generated from a uniform distribution on the interval [0, 3] and rounded to the nearest hundredth of an inch. The values appear in the order recorded (reading left to right, top to bottom). Note: the number of drops is stylized for classroom use — a real string this size would be struck by only a few drops per minute.</para>
      <table summary="" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="10">
          <colspec colnum="1" colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colnum="2" colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colnum="3" colname="c3"/>
          <colspec colnum="4" colname="c4"/>
          <colspec colnum="5" colname="c5"/>
          <colspec colnum="6" colname="c6"/>
          <colspec colnum="7" colname="c7"/>
          <colspec colnum="8" colname="c8"/>
          <colspec colnum="9" colname="c9"/>
          <colspec colnum="10" colname="c10"/>
          <tbody>
          <row><entry>0.24</entry><entry>1.72</entry><entry>0.36</entry><entry>1.52</entry><entry>2.94</entry><entry>1.50</entry><entry>1.85</entry><entry>1.72</entry><entry>2.87</entry><entry>1.37</entry></row>
          <row><entry>2.83</entry><entry>0.84</entry><entry>1.52</entry><entry>1.48</entry><entry>0.96</entry><entry>1.22</entry><entry>2.33</entry><entry>2.27</entry><entry>0.48</entry><entry>2.15</entry></row>
          <row><entry>1.29</entry><entry>1.14</entry><entry>1.07</entry><entry>2.10</entry><entry>1.23</entry><entry>0.59</entry><entry>2.70</entry><entry>0.87</entry><entry>2.13</entry><entry>2.66</entry></row>
          <row><entry>1.64</entry><entry>0.58</entry><entry>0.30</entry><entry>1.43</entry><entry>2.38</entry><entry>0.44</entry><entry>0.33</entry><entry>0.98</entry><entry>0.96</entry><entry>2.26</entry></row>
          <row><entry>1.38</entry><entry>1.21</entry><entry>2.85</entry><entry>1.30</entry><entry>0.67</entry><entry>2.29</entry><entry>1.72</entry><entry/><entry/><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Data Set B: Jalen Brunson — Points per Game, 2025–26 Season</title>
      <para id="para-00004">Data type: COLLECTED — this data was drawn from real, published, or personally logged records.</para>
      <para id="para-00005"><link url="https://openstax.org/r/stats-excel-data-set-b">Link to Excel Version of Data</link></para>
      <para id="para-00006">Points scored by Jalen Brunson (New York Knicks) in each of the 93 games he played during the 2025–26 season — 74 regular-season games and 19 playoff games (marked with an asterisk (*)). Values read left to right, top to bottom, in chronological order. The NBA Cup championship game (December 16, 2025) is excluded, consistent with official NBA statistics, which do not count that game toward regular-season totals.</para>
      <table summary="" id="table-00002">
        <tgroup cols="10">
          <colspec colnum="1" colname="c1"/>
          <colspec colnum="2" colname="c2"/>
          <colspec colnum="3" colname="c3"/>
          <colspec colnum="4" colname="c4"/>
          <colspec colnum="5" colname="c5"/>
          <colspec colnum="6" colname="c6"/>
          <colspec colnum="7" colname="c7"/>
          <colspec colnum="8" colname="c8"/>
          <colspec colnum="9" colname="c9"/>
          <colspec colnum="10" colname="c10"/>
          <tbody>
          <row><entry>23</entry><entry>31</entry><entry>37</entry><entry>36</entry><entry>29</entry><entry>31</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>23</entry><entry>19</entry><entry>32</entry></row>
          <row><entry>31</entry><entry>28</entry><entry>33</entry><entry>27</entry><entry>33</entry><entry>37</entry><entry>18</entry><entry>15</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>33</entry></row>
          <row><entry>30</entry><entry>35</entry><entry>40</entry><entry>25</entry><entry>22</entry><entry>47</entry><entry>34</entry><entry>34</entry><entry>28</entry><entry>29</entry></row>
          <row><entry>24</entry><entry>31</entry><entry>25</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>27</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>4</entry><entry>22</entry><entry>20</entry><entry>31</entry></row>
          <row><entry>28</entry><entry>13</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>12</entry><entry>21</entry><entry>42</entry><entry>12</entry><entry>31</entry><entry>40</entry><entry>8</entry></row>
          <row><entry>33</entry><entry>20</entry><entry>19</entry><entry>20</entry><entry>27</entry><entry>24</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>9</entry><entry>24</entry></row>
          <row><entry>28</entry><entry>28</entry><entry>29</entry><entry>30</entry><entry>17</entry><entry>23</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>26</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>12</entry></row>
          <row><entry>17</entry><entry>30</entry><entry>25</entry><entry>29</entry><entry>28*</entry><entry>29*</entry><entry>26*</entry><entry>19*</entry><entry>39*</entry><entry>17*</entry></row>
          <row><entry>35*</entry><entry>26*</entry><entry>33*</entry><entry>22*</entry><entry>38*</entry><entry>19*</entry><entry>30*</entry><entry>15*</entry><entry>30*</entry><entry>20*</entry></row>
          <row><entry>32*</entry><entry>36*</entry><entry>45*</entry><entry/><entry/><entry/><entry/><entry/><entry/><entry/></row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <para id="para-00007">* = playoff game.</para>
    </section>
